/* ==================================================================
   S C O P ' D
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   Black Ops II  //  Cronus Zen / GPC                     v2.0
   SNIPER BUILD  -  OFFLINE / BOT LOBBY / CAMPAIGN
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   MENU        : hold L2 + tap OPTIONS
   MASTER KILL : hold L2 + tap SHARE
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   v2.0 - TRICKSHOT ENGINE REWRITE

   The v1 macros were combos, and a combo is a straight line: every
   wait() pushes the next thing later. That is why they felt slow and
   why nothing happened "at the same time" - the spin could not start
   until the cancel had finished.

   v2 replaces them with a TIME-WINDOW SEQUENCER. A trickshot compiles
   into a set of independent (start,end) windows, one per control
   track, and ts_run() walks them every VM tick. Tracks overlap
   freely, so the spin runs THROUGH the jump and the YY instead of
   after them. Total length is now the longest track, not the sum.

   NOTHING TOUCHES L2 OR R2. No auto-scope, no auto-fire. The macro
   choreographs the movement and the cancels; you scope and you shoot.

   Every gap is tunable on TS TIMING - see the README.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   GPC NOTES: no local variables - all working vars are top level,
   prefixed by owner. Combos take set_val/wait only, no branching,
   which is exactly why the sequencer lives in a function instead.
   print() takes a data-section address, not a literal; no %d.

   SCREEN BUDGET (128 x 64, small font 7px wide / 8px tall):
     header y 0..11 | rows y 15,25,35,45,55 | labels x 3 (10 chars)
     values x 76 (6 chars) | scrollbar x 121..125
   ================================================================== */


